{title: Meant for Good}
{subtitle: Genesis 50:19–21; 37:3–28; 39:2–23; 41:25–43; 45:1–5}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 102}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Seventeen with a head full of [Bb]dreams
[Gm]Sheaves in the field bowing [F]down to me
Wore my [Eb]father's robe in the [Bb]morning sun
[Gm]Didn't see the anger I'd be[F]gun
[Eb]Down in a dry pit [Gm]under the sky
Twenty [F]pieces of silver and a caravan goodbye
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
A [Eb]slave in a stranger's [Gm]house
A [Bb]prisoner in [F]chains
But [Eb]the LORD was with Joseph
Through [Gm]the long and lonely [F]days
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You intended evil against [Eb]me
But God intended it for [Bb]good
Every pit and every pri[Gm]son
Brought me where I [F]stood
Now I see it from the pa[Eb]lace
What I never under[Gm]stood
You intended evil against [F]me
But God intended it for good [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Pharaoh dreamed of cattle and of [Bb]seven ears of grain
[Gm]Seven years of plenty, then [F]seven years of pain
They [Eb]called me from the prison to [Gm]stand before the throne
And [F]all the land of Egypt was put under my hand alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Brothers came for bread and [Gm]bowed down to the ground
[F]Just like in the dream, the sheaves had all come round
[Eb]I am Joseph, [Gm]your brother
[F]Come closer to me
[Eb]Do not be dis[Gm]tressed
God [F]sent me ahead of you to preserve [Eb]life
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You intended evil against me
But God intended it for [Bb]good
Every pit and every pri[Gm]son
Brought me where I [F]stood
Now I see it from the pa[Eb]lace
What I never under[Gm]stood
You intended evil against [F]me
But God intended it for good
{end_of_chorus}

